title: The Leipzig Congress
subtitle: The party congress meets to elect the Zentrale for the year of crisis.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1923 and month = 1 and ruhr_occupied = 1 and congress = 0
max-visits: 1
priority: 2
on-arrival: {!
Q.e23_lz_council = (Q.ultraleft_gone == 0 && Q.ultraleft_strength >= 10) ? 1 : 0;
Q.e23_lz_radek = (typeof Q.comintern_rep === 'string' && Q.comintern_rep.indexOf('Radek') >= 0) ? 1 : 0;
// the record of 1922 is in the delegates' pockets before the first session
var right = 0, left = 0;
if (Q.e22_fourth_congress == 1) { right += 0.04; }
if (Q.e22_fourth_congress == 2) { left += 0.05; }
if (Q.e22_saxon_toleration == 1 || Q.e22_saxon_toleration == 3) { right += 0.04; }
if (Q.e22_saxon_toleration == 2) { left += 0.03; }
if (Q.e22_rathenau_front == 1) { right += 0.03; }
if (Q.e22_rathenau_front == 2 || Q.e22_rathenau_front == 3) { left += 0.03; }
if (Q.e22_year_line == 1) { right += 0.02; }
if (Q.e22_year_line == 3) { left += 0.02; }
if (Q.e23_ruhr_line == 3) { left += 0.04; }
if (Q.e23_ruhr_line == 1) { right += 0.02; }
right += Math.max(-0.03, Math.min(0.04, (Q.spd_relation - 30) / 400));
left += Math.max(0, Math.min(0.05, (Q.militancy - 50) / 300));
Q.e23_lz_right_pull = right;
Q.e23_lz_left_pull = left;
Q.e23_lz_record = right > left + 0.03 ? 1 : (left > right + 0.03 ? 2 : 0);
RG.news('Party congress opens in Leipzig as French troops hold Essen', 2);
!}

= The Leipzig Congress

On 28 January, with French soldiers in Essen, the party's Eighth Congress meets in Leipzig to elect the Zentrale that will lead it through 1923.

[? if unionist_gone = 0 : Heinrich Brandler, a stonemason from the Chemnitz building trades, has written theses on the lines of the Fourth Congress: the united front, control committees in every works, and a workers' government with the SPD wherever there is a majority for one, beginning in Saxony. ?][? if offensive_gone = 0 : Ruth Fischer and Arkadi Maslow speak for Berlin, Ernst Thälmann for Hamburg. They say the Ruhr is burning and the Zentrale is writing letters to Dresden. ?][? if luxemburgist_gone = 0 : Between them sit Ernst Meyer, Wilhelm Pieck and Hugo Eberlein, who think both camps are half right and say so. ?][? if luxemburg_alive = 1 : Rosa Luxemburg will speak on the second day. ?]

[? if e23_lz_record = 1 : The delegates were elected after a year of the united front, and many of them liked it. ?][? if e23_lz_record = 2 : The delegates were elected in a year of anger, and the Ruhr has made them angrier. ?][? if e22_berlin_opposition = 1 : The Berlin delegates have not forgotten who took their leaders' posts in October. ?]

- @right: Fight for Brandler's theses.
- @middle: Put a motion of the centre.
- @left: Fight for the Left's theses.
- @council: Back the council communists.

@right
subtitle: [? if lead_code = 3 : The Zentrale defends its own line. ?] Moscow leans the same way.
view-if: unionist_gone = 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.e23_lz_backing = 'unionist';
Q.lean_unionist += 2;
if (Q.leading_faction != 'unionist') { Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 6; }
!}

- @open: The congress opens.

@middle
subtitle: The weakest motion at the start, and the one both camps could live with.
view-if: luxemburgist_gone = 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.e23_lz_backing = 'luxemburgist';
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 2;
if (Q.leading_faction != 'luxemburgist') { Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 6; }
!}

- @open: The congress opens.

@left
subtitle: Berlin, Hamburg and the Ruhr are behind it. Brandler's Saxons will fight.
view-if: offensive_gone = 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.e23_lz_backing = 'offensive';
Q.lean_offensive += 2;
if (Q.leading_faction != 'offensive') { Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 6; }
!}

- @open: The congress opens.

@council
subtitle: Out of the unions and the parliaments. They need every vote.
view-if: ultraleft_gone = 0
choose-if: e23_lz_council = 1
unavailable-subtitle: The council communists are too few to put a motion.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e23_lz_backing = 'ultraleft';
Q.lean_ultraleft += 2;
if (Q.leading_faction != 'ultraleft') { Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 6; }
!}

- @open: The congress opens.

@open
title: The Delegates Take Their Seats
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
var pos = ['unionist', 'offensive', 'luxemburgist'];
if (Q.ultraleft_gone == 0 && (Q.ultraleft_strength >= 10 || Q.e23_lz_backing == 'ultraleft')) { pos.push('ultraleft'); }
RG.congressStart({
    id: 'leipzig',
    name: 'The Leipzig Congress',
    stake: 'Who leads the party through 1923',
    sessions: 3,
    positions: pos,
    backing: Q.e23_lz_backing,
    kind: 'leadership',
    mandates: 'members',
    ownClose: true
});
if (Q.congress_leipzig == 1) {
    if (Q.unionist_gone == 0 && Q.e23_lz_right_pull > 0) { RG.congress.swayTo('unionist', Q.e23_lz_right_pull); }
    if (Q.offensive_gone == 0 && Q.e23_lz_left_pull > 0) { RG.congress.swayTo('offensive', Q.e23_lz_left_pull); }
    if (Q.e22_berlin_opposition == 1) { RG.congress.bitter(3); }
    RG.congress.tally();
}
!}

= The Delegates Take Their Seats

The mandate commission seats [+ congress_delegates_total +] delegates on the first morning. The first count gives the [+ congress_leader_name +] [+ congress_leader_votes +] per cent of the hall. [? if congress_ahead = 1 : Our motion leads, for now. ?][? if congress_ahead = 0 and congress_votes_for > 0 : Our motion has [+ congress_votes_for +] per cent. ?][? if congress_ahead = 0 and congress_votes_for = 0 : As things stand our motion would not survive the first ballot. ?]

Three days of sessions remain before the vote.
